      deepMeaning: "This parabolic potential energy well is the hallmark of simple harmonic motion. The force is always directed toward the minimum of the parabola — the equilibrium point. The shape of this potential well is universal: any smooth potential minimum looks parabolic for small displacements, which is why Hooke's Law and simple harmonic motion are so ubiquitous in nature.",
      derivation: "W = ∫₀ˣ kx' dx' = ½kx². The work done against the spring's restoring force equals the energy stored in the spring.",
