      misconception: "Common misconception: students often use PE = kx instead of PE = ½kx², forgetting the factor of ½. This factor arises because the force is not constant — it starts at zero and increases linearly with displacement. The work done is the area of a triangle under the force-displacement graph, which is ½ × base × height = ½ × x × kx = ½kx². Using PE = kx overestimates the stored energy by a factor of 2.",
