      misconception: "Common misconception: the ideal gas law applies only when temperature is in Kelvin (absolute), not Celsius. Using T in Celsius gives completely wrong results. Also, real gases deviate significantly from PV = nRT at high pressures (molecules are not point masses) and low temperatures (intermolecular attractions become important). The ideal gas law is an approximation — it fails whenever the assumptions of zero molecular volume and zero intermolecular forces break down.",
