      deepMeaning: "Latent heat is hidden energy — the word latent means hidden. When water boils at 100°C, you can keep adding heat indefinitely and the temperature stays at 100°C until all the water has vaporised. The energy goes into breaking hydrogen bonds between water molecules, not into increasing kinetic energy. The latent heat of vaporisation of water (2.26 × 10⁶ J/kg) is enormous — this is why sweating cools you so effectively, and why steam burns are far more severe than boiling water burns at the same temperature.",
