      misconception: "Common misconception: the T⁴ dependence is often under-appreciated in its steepness. Doubling temperature does not double radiated power — it multiplies it by 16 (2⁴). This is why the Sun, only about 20 times hotter than a warm room-temperature object, radiates incomparably more power. Also, P = εσAT⁴ gives the total power radiated — the net power exchanged between a body at temperature T and its surroundings at T₀ is P_net = εσA(T⁴ − T₀⁴). Students often forget the T₀⁴ subtraction term when calculating radiative cooling.",
      dimensions: "[M][T]⁻³  (power per unit area; σ has dimensions [M][T]⁻³[Θ]⁻⁴)",
