      deepMeaning: "Energy oscillates between the capacitor's electric field (½CV²) and the inductor's magnetic field (½LI²), just as in a mass-spring system energy oscillates between potential and kinetic. The analogy is mathematically exact: C ↔ 1/k (spring), L ↔ m (mass), Q ↔ x, I ↔ v. Equation of motion: L d²Q/dt² + Q/C = 0, identical to m d²x/dt² + kx = 0. In a real circuit, resistance causes damping — oscillations decay with time constant 2L/R.",
      derivation: "KVL: L dI/dt + Q/C = 0. Since I = dQ/dt: L d²Q/dt² + Q/C = 0 → d²Q/dt² = −Q/(LC) = −ω²Q, so ω = 1/√(LC).",
      whoDiscovered: "Theorised by Lord Kelvin in 1853 and demonstrated experimentally by Heinrich Hertz in 1887, producing the first artificial radio waves.",
      whyItMatters: "LC oscillators are the basis of all radio and wireless communication — every transmitter and receiver selects frequencies via LC resonance. Crystal oscillators (high-Q LC equivalent) provide precise timing in all computers, phones, and GPS receivers.",
