      deepMeaning: "From qvB = mv²/r: r = mv/(qB) — cyclotron radius, proportional to speed. Period T = 2πr/v = 2πm/(qB) — independent of speed. Faster particles orbit in larger circles but take the same time. This isochronous property enables the cyclotron accelerator: an oscillating electric field stays in sync with particles as they spiral outward gaining energy. At relativistic speeds, m → γm lowers the frequency — requiring the synchrotron design (LHC) where B increases with energy.",
      derivation: "Centripetal = magnetic force: mv²/r = qvB → r = mv/(qB). Period: T = 2πr/v = 2πm/(qB). Frequency: f = qB/(2πm). Angular frequency: ω_c = qB/m.",
